      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "2120484246401777737",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "@GoogleDeepMind @signalapp Verifying the compiled binary rather than a protocol model is what matters for shipped firmware. My open question is how the spec handles the boundary with the OS and driver code that moves keys in and out — that's usually where real-world assumptions leak in.",
      "url": "https://x.com/sunder0yct/status/2120639709911421369"
